      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          NSF Certified for Sport is the strictest widely available certification for protein powder in the US: it checks that the label is accurate, screens for contaminants, audits the factory, and tests for a panel of about 290 substances banned in sport. It is not the same as NSF Contents Certified, which verifies contents and contaminants but does not screen for banned substances, or NSF GMP Registration, which covers the factory but not the product. For most buyers the best NSF certified protein powder is Thorne Whey Protein Isolate, with Klean Isolate for an unflavored option, Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard (in its two certified flavors) on a budget, and Vega Sport for plant-based. Every pick below was looked up in the NSF Certified for Sport registry on November 8, 2026, and we list the exact flavors we found, because certification is granted product by product and sometimes flavor by flavor.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

