              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                NSF Contents Certified verifies label accuracy and screens for contaminants, which is valuable, but it does not test for banned substances. If you are drug tested, you need the Certified for Sport mark or an equivalent such as Informed Sport.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting a marketplace listing over the registry</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Product listings and retailer descriptions sometimes claim certifications that are out of date or apply to a different version. The registry is the source of truth. If a product is not listed, treat it as uncertified, however the listing reads.
